{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-24T21:26:40.935Z","data":{"text":"I've completed task 1 of the change. Summary:\n\n## What I built\n\n**New modules under `src/core/spec/`:**\n\n- **`lint-findings.ts`** — `LintFinding` (`severity`, `file`, `requirement`, `section`, `message`), `makeFinding`, the shared `openSpecSeverity` classifier, and `LintFindingSet` which keeps the change's own findings separate from `repository` and derives the legacy `errors`/`warnings` arrays from own findings only.\n- **`openspec-issues.ts`** — `parseOpenSpecItems` reads OpenSpec `items`; `scanOpenSpecIssues` maps each issue to a finding, resolves `requirements[<index>]` against the living spec via `parseCapabilitySpec`, reads change-issue requirement names from `ADDED \"<name>\"`-style messages, attributes own vs repository, and appends the unsupported-`skip_specs` note. Shared `execFileCapture` lives here.\n- **`merged-spec-check.ts`** — writes every mergable delta's `mergeDelta` output into one temp tree, validates it once with the real `openspec validate --specs --strict --json --no-interactive` (`OPENSPEC_TELEMETRY=0`, configured timeout), removes the folder, and omits inherited living-spec issues.\n\n**`linter.ts`** now builds findings for every check with repository-relative files, adds `findings`/`repository` to `LintResult`, makes `valid` depend only on own errors, names the linted change to `validateWithOpenSpec`, and runs merged validation through `verifyDeltaTargets`.\n\n**Tests:** new `tests/lint-findings.test.ts` (9 tests using the repository's real OpenSpec binary, asserting fields for every ADDED scenario except the three output ones). Updated the one pinned assertion in `tests/linter.test.ts`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/lint-findings.test.ts` — 9/9 pass.\n- Full `pnpm verify` — typechecks, build, entire suite, and lint pass.\n- Line/function budgets pass; no file outside scope was touched.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/075-lint-findings-you-can-act-on/.run/results/1.md`."}}
